Z||000000||PearlBlueSoul||12-19-2000||08:01 PM||||Hey, go ahead and lock this down if you want, cliff.  That's cool about the prior post too, i uderstand completely. <P>I'm just letting you guys know that I'm trying to sort this whole mess out with Cutter.  He seems to be foggy on a few things so I'm going through and correcting them.  So you can see the progress, I've posted a link to the thread.  DO NOT POST ON THIS THREAD.  I"m not interested in starting another flame.  It's being taken care of, and I'm only posting this so you guys can have some satisfaction that the MR2 group isn't taking this lightly. <BR> <A HREF="http://board.mr2pages.com/showthread.php?postid=49987#post49987" TARGET=_blank>http://board.mr2pages.com/showthread.php?postid=49987#post49987</A> <P>Remember:  NO POSTS from the Fiero crews.  I'm sure you guys already know the volatility of this situation so I need not say more.  Read on if you wish, I'm stickin up for you guys.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
